<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.7.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02203</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.7.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>bcb25926-f6fb-4732-9b57-62e61c88e311</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice">
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <exercise id="effa51f0-de35-4b1e-baca-468e423abcd4" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>For questions 1 – 7, find the factored form of the quadratic expression.</para>
          <para>\(x^2+4x − 12\)</para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para>\((x − 2)(x − 6)\)</para>
          <para>\((x + 3)(x − 4)\)</para>
          <para>\((x + 2)(x − 6)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 2)(x + 6)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.7.2.</para>
          <para>The correct answer is \((x − 2)(x + 6)\). </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_541f6352-18b0-4797-8c08-9ab7db738202" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>\(x^2−3x −18\)</para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para>\((x − 9)(x + 2)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 6)(x + 3)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 18)(x + 1)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 7)(x + 3)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.7.2.</para>
          <para>The correct answer is \((x − 6)(x + 3)\). </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_4fe26458-f975-4deb-ad0b-d7c70c4c76b7" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>\(x^2− 12x − 45\)</para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para>\((x − 45)(x + 1)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 8)(x − 4)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 9)(x + 5)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 15)(x + 3)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.7.2.</para>
          <para>The correct answer is \((x − 15)(x + 3)\). </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="c2b8d400-0602-4f65-8025-e9164acf0ba1" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>\(x^2−x −20\)</para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para>\((x − 10)(x + 2)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 5)(x + 4)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 20)(x + 1)\)</para>
          <para>\((x + 5)(x − 4)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.7.2.</para>
          <para>The correct answer is \((x − 5)(x + 4)\). </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_1f16b2c8-b765-4722-b7c2-c51b6c9597be" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>\(x^2+2x −35\)</para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para>\((x − 5)(x + 7)\)</para>
          <para>\((x + 5)(x + 7)\)</para>
          <para>\((x + 5)(x − 7)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 5)(x − 7)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.7.2.</para>
          <para>The correct answer is \((x − 5)(x + 7)\). </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_2e2b5660-6a28-47b3-a87b-41b819da8420" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>\(x^2−23x −50\)</para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para>\((x − 10)(x + 5)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 50)(x + 1)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 25)(x + 2)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 10)(x − 13)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.7.2.</para>
          <para>The correct answer is \((x − 25)(x + 2)\). </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_04fe1149-392c-4842-b320-5e6b70b1efcb" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>\(x^2+7x −60\)</para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para>\((x − 5)(x + 12)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 20)(x + 3)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 10)(x + 3)\)</para>
          <para>\((x − 4)(x + 15)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.7.2.</para>
          <para>The correct answer is \((x − 5)(x + 12)\). </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="f5493c4f-1803-422b-ae3a-97fcb91ff14c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>Consider the expression \(x^2+bx - 80\), where the leading coefficient equals 1. Identify all the pairs of factors of –80 that would result in positive values of \(b\).</para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para>80 and 1, 40 and 2, 20 and 4, 16 and 5, 10 and 8</para>
          <para>–80 and 1, –40 and 2, –20 and 4, –16 and 5, –10 and 8</para>
          <para>–80 and –1, –40 and –2, –20 and –4, –16 and –5, –10 and –8</para>
          <para>80 and –1, 40 and –2, 20 and –4, 16 and –5, 10 and -8</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.7.3. </para>
          <para>The correct answer is 80 and –1, 40 and –2, 20 and –4, 16 and –5, 10 and -8. </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_6bd4b83c-e264-4c0f-8a69-dad59273eff7" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>Consider the expression \(x^2+ bx - 80\), where the leading coefficient equals 1. Identify all the pairs of factors of –80 that would result in negative values of \(b\).</para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para>80 and 1, 40 and 2, 20 and 4, 16 and 5, 10 and 8</para>
          <para>–80 and 1, –40 and 2, –20 and 4, –16 and 5, –10 and 8</para>
          <para>–80 and –1, –40 and –2, –20 and –4, –16 and –5, –10 and –8</para>
          <para>80 and –1, 40 and –2, 20 and –4, 16 and –5, 10 and –8</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.7.3.</para>
          <para>The correct answer is –80 and 1, –40 and 2, –20 and 4, –16 and 5, –10 and 8.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_700e7afa-248a-463e-95a9-e0cd18635916" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>\(x^2\; \square \; 15x \;\square\; 34\) and \((x + 2)(x − 17)\)</para>
          <para>Here are pairs of equivalent expressions: one in standard form and the other in factored form. Identify the missing symbols:</para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para>– and –</para>
          <para>+ and –</para>
          <para>+ and +</para>
          <para>– and +</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.7.4.</para>
          <para>The correct answer is − and −.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
